# NOT the source of truth. On macOS the build "system layer" is defined by the
# recipes themselves (their `homebrew_formula:` fields plus the bits build-system
# base formulae), exactly the way packages/*.txt defines the Linux images. There
# is therefore no hand-maintained Brewfile here to drift out of sync.
#
# Generate the real, config-accurate Brewfile with bits — it scans the recipes
# your current configuration resolves and records the result in your local build
# area at <work-dir>/<arch>/Brewfile (work-dir defaults to ./sw):
#
#   bits brew -a osx_arm64            # or your osx_* architecture
#   brew bundle --file sw/osx_arm64/Brewfile
#
# Or let the build install formulae on demand:
#
#   bits build --brew ...            # runs `brew install <formula>` as needed
#
# Prerequisite bits does NOT install for you: the Xcode Command Line Tools
# (`xcode-select --install`) — Apple clang + the macOS SDK, used by the clang
# axis (Apple clang versions do not map to LLVM majors; see clang-toolchain.sh).
